OneiOS, stack 555b13d (NativeMetal 935c468), patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0003: thread CPU samples only where a diagnostic
reads them.
Port of patches/NativeMetal/0005 (take18, cpu-samples-only-for-trace). Changed in the port: the gate is diag=1 itself
(SHENG_DIAG, in any process), not the render server's frame trace alone: a superset, so whatever 935c468 writes with diag=1
still has its samples; without diag=1 no process asks thread_info at a command buffer's creation, commit or wait. The render
pipeline's cost is taken for the journal alone, as before.
Switch: none (diag=1 is the base's). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=cpu-samples-only-for-diagnostics).

The header of the 624bab3 stack's patch (patches/NativeMetal/0005-cpu-samples-only-for-trace.patch), which says the what and the why:
| OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0005: the thread CPU samples only where the trace or the journal reads
| them.
| Upstream: none (OneiOS; upstream NativeMetal 935c468 still calls NBCost::now() unconditionally).
| What: threadCpuUs() returns 0 without asking thread_info unless traceWanted() (SHENG_DIAG in backboardd, the only reader:
| tracePush); render pipeline creation takes NBCost::now() (mach_thread_self, thread_info, task_info) only while the pipeline
| journal is on (log-gpu=1), as its second sample already was.
| Why: take17's iOS log has 20,072 "Sandbox: com.apple.WebKit.GPU deny(1) syscall-mig 254" (Sandbox.kext's kobject index
| 254 = MIG 3612 thread_info: two at each command buffer's creation and commit) and 416 "deny(1) syscall-mach 27"
| (thread_self_trap, one at each render pipeline): each a refused kernel call and a sandbox violation report (WebKit's iOS GPU
| profile allows neither: gpu-defines.sb syscall-mig-allowed and syscall-mach-allowed). Other processes paid the calls for
| nothing.
| Switch: none (no behaviour changes: the values were read only by the diagnostics). Removable: yes
| (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=cpu-samples-only-for-trace).

diff --git a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
index c932054..4f25b8b 100644
--- a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
+++ b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
@@ -225,7 +225,12 @@ static std::mutex gPriorityLock;
 // Every diagnostic of this process (the frame trace, the sampler, Turnip's pass stamps and submission ring, the runtime's stage ring) runs only
 // with SHENG_DIAG set, which the plugin sets from the boot argument diag=1 before the device opens (NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm).
 static bool diagOn() {static const bool on=getenv("SHENG_DIAG")!=nullptr;return on;}
+// The thread's CPU time for the diagnostics' records, 0 where none is written (OneiOS, patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0003). Every command
+// buffer's creation and commit, and each wait, asked thread_info: a MIG call to the kernel, which WebKit's GPU process may not make (its
+// sandbox's kernel MIG filter: take17's log has 20,072 'deny(1) syscall-mig 254', thread_info, each a violation report), and whose
+// answer only the frame trace and the timing records read, both written with diag=1 alone.
 static uint32_t threadCpuUs() {
+ if(!diagOn())return 0;
  thread_basic_info_data_t info;mach_msg_type_number_t count=THREAD_BASIC_INFO_COUNT;
  if(thread_info(pthread_mach_thread_np(pthread_self()),THREAD_BASIC_INFO,(thread_info_t)&info,&count)!=KERN_SUCCESS)return 0;
  return (uint32_t)((uint64_t)(info.user_time.seconds+info.system_time.seconds)*1000000ull+(uint64_t)(info.user_time.microseconds+info.system_time.microseconds));
@@ -5955,7 +5960,9 @@ static void computeRefused(id<MTLFunction> function,NSString *why) {
  std::vector<NmbBinaryArchive *> archives;
  if(!pipelineArchives(d.binaryArchives,archives,error)){delete p;return nil;}
  const NmbPipelineOptions creation={(uint64_t)options,archives.data(),archives.size()};
- const uint64_t pipelineBegan=nowUs();const NBCost costBegan=NBCost::now();
+ // OneiOS: the cost only for the journal, its one reader (NBCost::now asks mach_thread_self and thread_info: refused in WebKit's GPU
+ // process, take17's 416 'deny(1) syscall-mach 27', one at every render pipeline it made, and as many MIG reports).
+ const uint64_t pipelineBegan=nowUs();const NBCost costBegan=gJournalPath.empty()?NBCost():NBCost::now();
  uint64_t cacheBefore[10]={};if(!gJournalPath.empty())nmb_device_work_stats(gDevice,cacheBefore);
  NmbRenderPipeline *handle=nmb_render_pipeline_new_with_options(gDevice,p,&creation);
  __attribute__((objc_precise_lifetime)) MTLRenderPipelineDescriptor *retry=nil;
